<!--
  rev_review main form. Shape copied from Entities/rev_grant/FormXml/main/, which was itself
  copied from Entities/rev_errorlog/FormXml/main/ (live in REV-GrantApplications-DEV) - every
  control classid used below was harvested from a form live in that environment and matched to
  the attribute type it is used with, none is inferred (IMP-0014 shipped three dropdowns with no
  options from one guessed classid):

    plain single-line text   {4273EDBD-AC1D-40d3-9FB2-095C621B552D}  (rev_grant.rev_name)
    lookup                   {270BD3DB-D9AF-4782-9025-509E298DEC0A}  (rev_grant.rev_applicationid)
    picklist                 {3EF39988-22BB-4f0b-BBBE-64B5A3748AEE}  (rev_grant.rev_status)
    date / datetime          {5B773807-9FB2-42db-97C3-7A91EFF8ADFF}  (rev_grant.rev_holidaystart;
                              also rev_application.rev_scoredon/rev_overriddenon - the SAME
                              classid serves both DateOnly and full-datetime formats, confirmed
                              live via that form)
    multiline text (textarea) {E0DECE4B-6FC8-4a8f-A065-082708572369} (rev_grant.rev_conditions)

  The lookup classid is proven live only for a lookup TARGETING rev_application (rev_grant's
  own rev_applicationid control). rev_trustee1/rev_trustee2 target systemuser instead - the
  control classid identifies the LOOKUP CONTROL TYPE, not its target entity, which is a general
  Dataverse property rather than something specific to this solution, but it has not itself
  been confirmed against a systemuser-targeting lookup IN THIS SOLUTION. Flagged as A-REV-01 in
  the Dev Summary Unvalidated Assumptions Register (C-TECH-052) - cheapest verification: open
  this form in the maker portal after a live import and confirm the Trustee 1/Trustee 2 fields
  render as a working lookup picker rather than an empty or broken control.

  EVERY LABEL IS THE ATTRIBUTE'S OWN AUTHORED displayname, VERBATIM (IMP-0015 - no test asserts
  label text, so labels must be copied deliberately, not re-typed from memory).

  SECTION ORDER FOLLOWS THE PANEL'S OWN WORKFLOW: which application and when, then each
  trustee's independent verdict in turn, then the staff-facing resolution - so a screen-reader
  user meets the fields in the order the process uses them (TAD section 8), the same principle
  rev_grant's form comment records for the grant lifecycle.

  rev_notes1, rev_notes2 and rev_staffrecommendation carry auto="true" on the CELL (IMP-0127 -
  "use all available vertical space" on a multiline text field is a cell attribute, not a
  control property and not a rowspan) because their column Format is textarea (IMP-0128 - an
  nvarchar/ntext column renders multi-line only when ITS OWN Format is textarea; the form
  control alone cannot make that happen).

  rev_name and rev_finalisedon are disabled: one is platform-generated, the other is written
  only by the Finalise Decisions flow (WBS 6.6) - the same reasoning rev_grant's form applies
  to rev_docusignenvelopeid ("written only by the acceptance flow that WBS 3.2 will build").

  TRUSTEE WRITE SCOPE IS NOT ENFORCED BY THIS FORM. Every control below is enabled except the
  two named above - "Trustees write verdict and notes only" (TAD section 3.1, FR-037) is a
  security-role field-permission decision for WBS 6.1's REV Trustee role, out of this session's
  scope (Roles/ is untouched here). A trustee's actual write surface on this table is narrower
  than what this form technically allows an ADMIN to edit.
-->
